%N A400700 Start with a set of four adjacent collinear points in a hexagonal lattice. Every iteration, add to the set the points in the lattice which are adjacent to at least two points already in the set. This sequence gives the number of points in the set after n iterations.
%H A400700 Aidan Markey, <a href="/A400700/a400700.pdf">Illustration of initial terms</a>
%H A400700 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (2,-1,1,-2,1).
%F A400700 a(n) = (3n^2 + 13n + 12 + 2 * (n mod 3))/3.
%F A400700 From _Sean A. Irvine_, Oct 09 2026: (Start)
%F A400700 a(n) = 2*a(n-1) - a(n-2) + a(n-3) - 2*a(n-4) + a(n-5).
%F A400700 G.f.: 2 * (2+x+x^2-2*x^3+x^4) / ((1-x^3) * (1-x)^2)). (End)
%e A400700 See Links.
%Y A400700 Cf. A374338, A400699, A400701 (corresponding sequences for two, three, and five points).
%Y A400700 Cf. A008458, A338097.
%K A400700 nonn,new
%O A400700 0,1
%A A400700 _Aidan Markey_, Oct 03 2026
%E A400700 More terms from _Sean A. Irvine_, Oct 09 2026
